@startuml career_classes
title Career (tp::career): the ladder of rungs (a class at a level) and the titles that climb it
hide empty members
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "other components" {
  class "season::Standing" as SeasonStanding
  class "event::kMaxPullers" as MaxPullers
}

package "tp::career" {
  class Ladder <<struct>> {
    +rungs : int
    +promotion_place : int
    +min_seasons : int
  }
  class Progress <<struct>> {
    +rung : int
    +unlocked : int
    +seasons : int
    +title : bool
  }
  class "career functions" as CareerFns <<free functions>> {
    +kMaxRungs = 36
    +kMaxMinSeasons = 10
    +validate(const Ladder&) : optional<ParamError>
    +valid(const Progress&, const Ladder&) : bool
    +starting_at(const Ladder&, rung) : optional<Progress>
    +finish_season(Progress&, const Ladder&, championship_place) : bool
    +finish_season(Progress&, const Ladder&, span<const season::Standing>, player) : bool
    +may_move_up(const Progress&) : bool
    +move_up(Progress&) : bool
  }
  CareerFns ..> Ladder
  CareerFns ..> Progress
}
CareerFns ..> SeasonStanding : the player's place\nin the championship
CareerFns ..> MaxPullers : a promotion place\na field can have
note bottom of Progress
  a rung is a class at one of its levels (belofte, promo, top).
  A season finished at promotion_place or better (1: the title)
  opens the rung above once the rung has had min_seasons seasons
  (a title in the first opens it after the last of them); the
  player is asked whether to move up.
  A rung opened stays open: a player who stays to defend the
  title may move up after a later season. starting_at() starts a
  career on any rung, for testing. Which rung is which (season,
  garage, rules) is the data's (data/careers/)
end note
@enduml
